# PORT playbook (fewer prompts)

Jira MCP namespace: `user-Atlassian`. Site/cloudId: `https://shubhamshindeinbox.atlassian.net`. Project: **PORT**.

## Cut approvals (you, one time)

Cursor cannot skip MCP/shell prompts unless you allow them:

1. **Cursor Settings → Agents → Auto-run** (or Auto-run in chat): turn on for this repo.
2. **Cursor Settings → MCP → Atlassian**: enable **auto-run / allow without asking** for that server.

Until that is on, every `searchJiraIssuesUsingJql` / `createJiraIssue` / Shell call can pop **Yes**. The agent must still **batch** so you click once per turn, not 20 times.

## Agent: batch, do not rediscover

On `start` or any Jira work, **one turn** should be enough for lookup:

- `searchJiraIssuesUsingJql` with  
  `jql`: `project = PORT AND (sprint in openSprints() OR sprint in futureSprints())`  
  `fields`: `summary,status,issuetype,description,assignee,customfield_10020`  
  `maxResults`: 20  
- Do **not** also call `getVisibleJiraProjects`, dump the whole Atlassian catalog, or `getJiraIssue` unless the search row is not enough.
- Sprint field is `customfield_10020`. Planned sprint = `state: "future"`. `openSprints()` misses those.

After the PR exists, **one turn** for Jira wrap-up (parallel):

- `transitionJiraIssue` id **21** = In Progress, **31** = Done (PORT team-managed).
- `addWorklogToJiraIssue` (`timeSpent` e.g. `15m`)
- `addCommentToJiraIssue` (PR URL)
- `createIssueLink` `type`: `Relates`
- `createJiraIssue` only for backlog follow-ups (max 10). Epic parent: `additional_fields: { "parent": { "key": "PORT-6" } }`

## Ticket links

In PR title/body and chat, always:

`[PORT-13](https://shubhamshindeinbox.atlassian.net/browse/PORT-13)`

## Sprint vs backlog

`customfield_10020` empty or missing = **backlog**. Do not implement. Tell the user with a link and wait for them to add it to a sprint.

`createJiraIssue` follow-ups stay in backlog. Do not then code those issues in the same run.

## GitHub: what works vs what fails

**Works**

- `git push -u origin HEAD`
- `gh pr create` (REST create)
- `gh api repos/Shubham-code-lab/Portfolio-v2/pulls?state=all&per_page=1` — latest PR number; next is that + 1 for `release.json` `pr` before first push.
- Commit author via env `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME` / `GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL` (never `git config`)
- PowerShell: `;` not `&&`

**Fails — do not retry**

- `gh pr view --json reviewRequests` and `gh pr edit`: GraphQL needs `read:org`; token only has `repo`.
- `--reviewer Shubham-code-lab` on your own PR: GitHub blocks self-review. Put the reviewer in the PR body only.
- `npm` without fnm PATH in old terminals.

## Do not

- Serial “list tools → get schema → search → get project → get issue → get transitions” for the same ticket.
- Ask the user to approve the same failed `gh` GraphQL call again.
